<title>UK: UK Conservatives vow gas, water competition push.</title>
<headline>UK Conservatives vow gas, water competition push.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's ruling Conservative party said on Wednesday it intended to introduce competition in the water industry and reaffirmed intentions to open up the domestic gas market.</p>
<p>Launching the party's manifesto for the May 1 election on Wednesday, the Conservatives said &quot;we will extend competition for domestic gas users and introduce competition in the water industry, starting with large users.&quot;</p>
<p>The gas industry is scheduled for liberalisation, including for domestic users, by 1998 along with electricity supply.</p>
<p>The water industry is testing out methods for competition for large users and the watchdog body Ofwat is currently considering 18 applications for so-called &quot;inset&quot; appointments, where a large user is provided with water services from a supplier outside the area.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44171 542 7717</p>
